<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>org.gnome.gnome-commander</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0+</project_license>
  <name>Gnome Commander</name>
  <summary>Dual-panel file manager</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Gnome Commander is a “dual-panel” graphical file manager.
      It features separate tabs for each panel,
      setting up custom device buttons, bookmark manager, fully integrated
      commandline, file quick search, an internal image viewer, a powerful
      batch renaming tool, and FTP and Samba access.
    </p>
    <p>
      Gnome Commander aims to advanced users who like to focus on precise
      file management, working in parallel through special applications,
      and running smart commands.
    </p>
  </description>
  <kudos>
    <kudo>UserDocs</kudo>
  </kudos>
  <keywords>
    <keyword>file manager</keyword>
    <keyword>file system</keyword>
    <keyword>SSH</keyword>
    <keyword>FTP</keyword>
    <keyword>WebDAV</keyword>
  </keywords>
  <screenshots>
    <screenshot type="default">
      <image>https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-commander/-/raw/pages/public/images/screenshot-1024-light.png</image>
    </screenshot>
  </screenshots>
  <url type="homepage">https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/gnome-commander/</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-commander/-/work_items</url>
  <url type="contribute">https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/gnome-commander/#contributing</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-commander</url>
  <update_contact>gcmd-devel_AT_nongnu.org</update_contact>
  <project_group>GNOME</project_group>
  <developer id="org.gnome">
    <name>The Gnome Commander team</name>
  </developer>
  <translation type="gettext">gnome-commander</translation>
  <content_rating type="oars-1.0" />
  <launchable type="desktop-id">org.gnome.gnome-commander.desktop</launchable>
  <provides>
    <binary>gnome-commander</binary>
    <id>gnome-commander.desktop</id>
  </provides>
  <suggests type="upstream">
    <id>org.gnome.meld.desktop</id>
    <id>org.gnome.Yelp</id>
  </suggests>

  <releases>
    <release type="stable" version="2.2.3" date="2026-11-11">
      <description>
        <p>This release includes the following features and changes:</p>
        <p>Issue #207: New plugin interface</p>
        <ul>
        <li>The interface is documented.</li>
        <li>New built-in plugins have similar but not identical functionality to the old ones.</li>
        <li>Built-in plugins are enabled automatically, user-installed plugins in <code>~/.config/gnome-commander/plugins</code> have to be enabled.</li>
        <li>Plugins can be written in any programming language.</li>
        <li>Python-based plugins can import <code>plugin_helper</code> module that makes implementation simpler.</li>
        <li>Issue #332: Context menu scripts are a plugin now. Also, new special comment <code>#single-file:true</code> indicates that the script should always be run for each file separately.</li>
        <li>Issue #333: Main menu actions of plugins can be assigned a keyboard shortcut via Keyboard Shortcuts dialog.</li>
        <li>Issue #340: Placing the mouse pointer above the file name in Plugins dialog will show the full path to the plugin.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Various improvements to the internal viewer</p>
        <ul>
        <li>Issue #383: Made all files show up as different tabs within a single viewer window</li>
        <li>Issue #273: Made case-insensitive search work with non-ASCII letters</li>
        <li>Issue #324: Remember window’s maximized state (AndriiC)</li>
        <li>Issue #336: Scroll automatically during selection if the mouse cursor moves out of the text</li>
        <li>Issue #370: Search defaults to the selected text</li>
        <li>Issue #371: Handle selection via double-click (word) or tripple-click (line)</li>
        <li>Issue #384: Search only continues from the selection if that selection is visible</li>
        <li>Issue #390: Improved guessing of preferable display mode when file is opened</li>
        <li>Implemented extending selection via Shift+Click</li>
        <li>Issue #401: Implemented extending selection via keyboard (e.g. Shift+Left or Shift+Page Down)</li>
        <li>Issue #424: Pressing Escape will close the search bar even if it isn’t focused.</li>
        <li>Issue #431: Added support for Ctrl+Left and Ctrl+Right keyboard shortcuts for faster horizontal navigation</li>
        <li>Issue #432: Line length in unwrapped Text mode has been restricted to 4096 characters to improve performance</li>
        <li>Issue #433: Made newline characters visible when they are selected</li>
        <li>Roughly factor 10 search performance improvement</li>
        <li>When opening viewer from the Search dialog, the search match is immediately selected</li>
        <li>Fixed handling of newlines in Text mode with CP437 encoding</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Improvements to handling of removable devices</p>
        <ul>
        <li>Issue #450: Eject devices when possible instead of merely unmounting them</li>
        <li>Issue #451: Fixed recognizing device removal</li>
        <li>Issue #452: Added support for MTP devices like smartphones</li>
        <li>Issue #453: Made sure selected connection reflects navigation in and out of a device mount directory</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Other features and changes</p>
        <ul>
        <li>Issue #367: Portable builds</li>
        <li>Issue #300: Added new “Copy File Paths” and “Copy File URIs” actions, their keyboard shortcuts can now be configured separately from “Copy File Names”.</li>
        <li>Issue #312: Improved file column management, allowing to reset column widths and apply current settings to all tabs</li>
        <li>Issue #318: File icon size is set automatically according to font size, the unused icon size and scale quality settings have been removed.</li>
        <li>Issue #322: Keep selected file on directory reload</li>
        <li>Issue #359: Made navigating back to a directory and switching to a different directory then produce the expected navigation history</li>
        <li>Issue #365: Quick Search is closed when current directory changes</li>
        <li>Issue #366: When “Rename” action is chosen on file name conflict, renaming keeps file extension now</li>
        <li>Keyboard shortcuts can now be assigned to bookmarks via Keyboard Shortcuts dialog.</li>
        <li>Issue #372, #382, #392: Made displaying directory changes (files added, removed, renamed) more consistent and a whole lot faster</li>
        <li>Issue #374: Open new file list tabs next to the current tab</li>
        <li>Issue #380: Renaming files will now offer the usual actions if this name already exists. Renaming files into a different directory is possible as well.</li>
        <li>Issue #398: Display a message when a command running in embedded terminal is done</li>
        <li>Issue #409: Made screen readers say whether a file is selected</li>
        <li>Issue #410: Added configurable Ctrl+Shift+F10 and Ctrl+Menu keyboard shortcuts to open file list header pop-up. Made Shift+F10 and Menu keyboard shortcuts configurable as well.</li>
        <li>Issue #413: Copy File in Current Directory action will now select the new file</li>
        <li>Issue #418: Improved interoperability of Drag &amp; Drop with other applications</li>
        <li>Issue #422: Starting Quick Search via non-ASCII letters is possible now.</li>
        <li>Issue #423: Pressing Escape will close Quick Search even if it isn’t focused.</li>
        <li>Issue #430: Special file permissions like suid are now displayed in all the relevant places, they are left unchanged when file permissions are modified</li>
        <li>Issue #440: Made Search dialog’s content search work without reading entire files into memory</li>
        <li>Issue #449: When main menu isn’t visible its contents are accessible via a button in the title bar</li>
        <li>Started migrating the code to a new component framework to improve maintainability and reliability</li>
        <li>Added hex search to Search dialog’s content search</li>
        <li>Listing a large directory no longer hangs Gnome Commander and can now be aborted</li>
        <li>Temporary network connections now show up in all device lists as long as they are open.</li>
        <li>Added keyboard mnemonics to some main menu items that didn’t have any.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This release fixes the following bugs:</p>
        <ul>
        <li>Issue #226: Allowed cancelling file transfers in the middle of a file</li>
        <li>Issue #301: Spell “KiB” correctly</li>
        <li>Issue #321: Only reload the destination of copy/move operation if it is a remote directory</li>
        <li>Issue #343: Made file context menu in Advanced Rename dialog apply to the file being right-clicked</li>
        <li>Issue #346: Made Ctrl+Tab/Ctrl+Shift+Tab switch tabs in File Properties dialog (Lukáš Tyrychtr)</li>
        <li>Issue #351: Fixed inconsistent updates when multiple directories are removed</li>
        <li>Issue #353: Made sure clicking device buttons doesn’t leave input focus there</li>
        <li>Issue #354: Made sure middle-clicking <code>..</code> opens a new tab (regression in Gnome Commander 2.0)</li>
        <li>Issue #355: Made closing duplicate tabs not leave unnecessary duplicates of locked tabs around</li>
        <li>Issue #360: <code>cd</code> command on a locked tab was affecting current tab instead of opening a new one</li>
        <li>Issue #361: Running <code>cd dir</code> on command line will no longer change input focus</li>
        <li>Issue #364: Navigation to a bookmark with a quoted name like <code>'test'</code> was failing</li>
        <li>Issue #369: Removed “case-sensitive sorting” option which wasn’t really working</li>
        <li>Issue #375: Made sure the Bookmarks submenu of the main menu updates on connection or bookmark changes</li>
        <li>Issue #391: Made file icon update when the file changes</li>
        <li>Issue #397: Do not attempt to calculate size of <code>..</code> directory</li>
        <li>Issue #402: Pressing Enter on a file will no longer run command line, only when command line is focused</li>
        <li>Issue #403: Fixed display of selected item in the search results list</li>
        <li>Issue #404: Fixed embedded terminal actions (Copy/Paste/Select All)</li>
        <li>Issue #405: Command line history wouldn’t open if some commands are very long</li>
        <li>Issue #406: Do not allow renaming <code>..</code></li>
        <li>Issue #407: Pressing Delete in a text field in the Search dialog no longer suggests deleting a file</li>
        <li>Issue #408: Fixed crash when copying files to a read-only file system and choosing “Replace All” (Lukáš Tyrychtr)</li>
        <li>Issue #411: Fixed input focus issues when closing a submenu of the file context menu</li>
        <li>Issue #417: Changes to format options apply immediately now</li>
        <li>Issue #426: Fixed internal viewer displaying and copying newlines as dots in ASCII mode</li>
        <li>Issue #427: Do not display file permissions for <code>..</code></li>
        <li>Issue #429: Display file’s context menu when right-clicking its icon</li>
        <li>Issue #435: Moving up in internal viewer while in wrapped text mode wouldn’t reach start of file</li>
        <li>Issue #436: Corrected mouse selection in internal viewer’s Fixed Width mode when tab characters are present</li>
        <li>Issue #438: Display selected tab characters with correct width in internal viewer’s Text mode</li>
        <li>Issue #444: Made search result selection in internal viewer work with invalid UTF-8 correctly</li>
        <li>Resolved keyboard mnemonics conflict in the File menu between “Search” and “Create Symbolic Link”</li>
        </ul>
        <p>New or updated translations: ca (Jordi Mas), cs (Patrik Sivek), de (Stefan), eu (Asier Saratsua Garmendia), ka (Ekaterine Papava), kk (Baurzhan Muftakhidinov), nb (Kjartan Maraas), ru (Sergej A.), sl (Martin), sr (Марко Костић), sv (Anders Jonsson), uk (Yuri Chornoivan)</p>
        <p>New or updated docs: hu (Balázs Úr), kk (Baurzhan Muftakhidinov), ru (Sergej A.), sv (Anders Jonsson)</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release type="stable" version="2.0.3" date="2026-06-13">
      <description>
        <p>This release fixes the following bugs:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Issue #347: JPEG images marked as rotated in metadata weren’t displayed rotated</li>
          <li>Issue #376: Search dialog: “Case sensitive” button for content search had reversed effect</li>
          <li>Issue #379: Size of the Search dialog wasn’t restored after restarting application</li>
          <li>Issue #385: Bogus keyboard input focus after clicking toolbar buttons</li>
          <li>Issue #386: File list theme wasn’t applied in the Search dialog</li>
          <li>Issue #377: Overlong contents in file list cells were cut off, not ellipsized</li>
          <li>Issue #388 and #389: Internal viewer: incorrect handling of the file start when searching for a single character backwards</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release type="stable" version="2.0.2" date="2026-06-01">
      <description>
        <p>This release fixes the following bugs:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Issue #345: The Copy button in the Copy File dialog wasn’t set as the default action</li>
          <li>Issue #356 and #357: Glitches displaying free space of the current volume</li>
          <li>Issue #358: Double-clicking tab area created a new tab but didn’t keep the selected file</li>
          <li>Issue #363: Switching tabs didn’t reset Quick Filter</li>
          <li>Issue #349 and #350: Incorrect logic determining when directory monitoring should be stopped</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release type="stable" version="2.0.1" date="2026-05-27">
      <description>
        <p>This release fixes the following bugs:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Issue #326: Right panel would occasionally occupy all available space on startup, rendering left panel invisible</li>
          <li>Color themes were broken with older Gtk versions (e.g. on Ubuntu 24.04)</li>
          <li>Issue #327: With older Gtk versions (e.g. on Ubuntu 24.04) clicking a device button only worked once (AndriiC)</li>
          <li>Issue #331: No Quit menu item in the File menu</li>
          <li>Issue #335: Running search for the first time would list home directory contents as “search results”</li>
          <li>Issue #334: Internal viewer doesn’t allow selecting the first character in a line (AndriiC)</li>
          <li>Issue #334: Moving mouse pointer out of the internal viewer window selects everything to the start of the visible area (AndriiC)</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release type="stable" version="2.0.0" date="2026-05-17">
      <description>
        <p>This release includes the following features and changes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Added embedded terminal to display output of commands run by Gnome Commander (see issue #213). The new “Hide Command Line Output When Inactive” in “View” menu hides the terminal automatically when inactive.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Redesigned Quick Search functionality:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Filtering the file list is now possible as well. The default mode can be configured in the Options dialog</li>
          <li>Text is always matched anywhere in the file name unless wildcard patterns `*` or `?` are used explicitly</li>
          <li>A button to enable case-sensitive matching has been added</li>
          <li>Quick Search no longer starts searching at the beginning of the file list but at the current position</li>
          <li>Most keyboard shortcuts can be used from Quick Search without causing it to close</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Various improvements to the Search dialog:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Improved performance</li>
          <li>Closing and re-opening search no longer clears the search results</li>
          <li>Path matching can now use extended glob expressions like dir/**/*.md that will be applied to the entire path relative to current directory</li>
          <li>A button to choose whether path matching should be case-sensitive has been added</li>
          <li>Search progress shows the directory currently being searched</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Various improvements to the internal viewer:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Viewer font can now be chosen from the Settings menu</li>
            <li>Binary mode has been renamed into Fixed Width and supports UTF-8</li>
            <li>Replaced the search dialog by a search bar</li>
            <li>Added support for case-insensitive hexadecimal search</li>
            <li>Considerably improved search performance</li>
            <li>Added “Select All” menu item for text</li>
            <li>Added a context menu for images</li>
            <li>Status bar displays some information for images as well now</li>
            <li>DOS-style CRLF line breaks are recognized as a single line break now</li>
            <li>Many bug fixes</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Other new features and improvements:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Migration of the overall codebase to the Rust language and Gtk4</li>
            <li>Updated the program license to GPL-3.0+</li>
            <li>Improved accessibility of the application, allowing screen readers to better recognize context (see issue #23)</li>
            <li>Redesigned Keyboard Shortcuts dialog, making it easier to use. Also, the list of configurable keyboard shortcuts has been vastly expanded.</li>
            <li>Switching tabs in Options dialog is now possible via Ctrl+Tab and Shift+Ctrl+Tab (see issue #254)</li>
            <li>Navigation history is no longer shared between different panels (see issue #49)</li>
            <li>External terminal application is now xdg-terminal-exec by default which will launch the configured default terminal</li>
            <li>Calculating size of a large directory will no longer hang up Gnome Commander, and selecting a different file will abort the operation in progress (see issue #9)</li>
            <li>Improved Wayland support, starting an application immediately activates it if the application supports this</li>
            <li>New option to treat symlinks as regular files (see issue #159)</li>
            <li>The “Search window is minimizable” option is now called “Search window always on top” and no longer requires a restart (see issue #236)</li>
            <li>Made the text indicating size and number of selected files easier to translate (see issue #176)</li>
            <li>When a command is run in an external terminal no additional pause is being added as the terminal application will usually leave the window open anyway</li>
            <li>Better icon for “Copy File Names” action that respects dark mode</li>
            <li>Added support for icon theme directories for MIME icons</li>
            <li>Order of columns in the file panels can now be altered by mouse drag-n-drop</li>
            <li>Removed the dependency on xpm library for MIME icons</li>
          </ul>
          <p>This release fixes the following bugs:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Various documentation mistakes correction (Anders Jonsson)</li>
            <li>Search is now stopped automatically when the Search dialog is closed</li>
            <li>Made sure that opening multiple dialogs of the same type is not possible, instead the existing dialog is brought up (see issue #234)</li>
            <li>Fixed issues when directory opened in one panel is renamed in another (see issue #229)</li>
            <li>Restoring remote connections on startup only succeeded for already active connections</li>
            <li>Remote connection restored on startup was lacking its bookmarks (see issue #217)</li>
            <li>Navigating history via file list’s dropdown no longer reorders history entries</li>
            <li>When ALT+letters was supposed to start Quick Search, they would occasionally open menu instead (see issue #204)</li>
            <li>No visual indication of file selection in “Respect theme’s colors” mode</li>
            <li>Switching tabs in the inactive panel wouldn’t activate it (see issue #216)</li>
            <li>Fixed search continuing in background when aborted</li>
            <li>Respect theme’s text color in the internal viewer, fixing display in dark mode (see issue #199)</li>
            <li>Renamed files were still displaying the old name (Andrey Kutejko)</li>
            <li>Device bar overflow is fixed when it exceeds the panel width</li>
            <li>Advanced rename dialog does not exceed screen size anymore for long file names</li>
            <li>Pressing the keypad button “*” does not select / deselect the “..” directory anymore</li>
            <li>Selected files in tabs are kept when switching tabs</li>
          </ul>
          <p>New or updated translations: ca (Jordi Mas), cs (Daniel Rusek), da (Alan Mortensen), el (Efstathios Iosifidis), es (Daniel Mustieles), eu (Asier Sarasua Garmendia), fr (Jean-Marc Tissières), hu (Balázs Úr), id (Andika Triwidada), ja (Oyamada Jun, Ryo Nakano), ka (Ekaterine Papava), kk (Baurzhan Muftakhidinov), pt (Hugo Carvalho), pt_BR (Juliano de Souza Camargo, Rafael Fontenelle, Álvaro Burns), ru (Sergej A.), sl (Martin), sr (Марко Костић, Мирослав Николић), sv (Anders Jonsson), tr (Emin Tufan Çetin, Sabri Ünal), uk (Yuri Chornoivan)</p>
          <p>New or updated docs: hu (Balázs Úr), kk (Baurzhan Muftakhidinov), ru (Sergej A.), sr (Марко Костић), sv (Anders Jonsson)</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release type="stable" version="1.18.6" date="2026-04-26">
      <description>
        <p>New or updated translations: kk (Baurzhan Muftakhidinov), sr (Марко Костић)</p>
